7–66. doi: 10.1016/j.jbi.2005.02.005. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 27. Cooper GF, Aliferis CF, Ambrosino R, et al. An evaluation of machine-learning methods for predicting pneumonia mortality. Artif Intell Med. 1997;9(2):107–38. doi: 10.1016/s0933-3657(96)00367-3. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 28. Miotto R, Li L, Kidd BA, Dudley JT. Deep patient: an unsupervised representation to predict the future of patients from the electronic health records. Sci Rep. 2016;6:26094. doi: 10.1038/srep26094. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 29. Knight W. The Dark Secret at the Heart of AI. MIT Technology Review. [Accessed on April 14, 2018]. Available at: https://www.technologyreview.com/s/604087/the-dark-secret-at-the-heart-of-ai/ 30. Wikipedia contributors. Natural language processing. Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia. [Accessed on December 21, 2018]. Available at: https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Natural_language_processing&oldid=872887903 . 31. Bahl LR, Jelinek F, Mercer RL. A maximum likelihood approach to continuous speech recognition. IEEE Trans Pattern Anal Mach Intell. 1983;5(2):179–90. doi: 10.1109/tpami.1983.4767370. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 32. Jurafsky D, Martin JH. Speech and Language Processing. Upper Saddle River, New Jersey: Prentice-Hall; 2000. [ Google Scholar ] 33. Manning C, Schuetze H. Foundations of Statistical Natural Language Processing. Cambridge, Massachusetts: MIT Press; 1999. [ Google Scholar ] 34. Kaur H, Sohn S, Wi CI, et al. Automated chart review utilizing natural language processing algorithm for asthma predictive index. BMC Pulm Med. 2018;18(1):34. doi: 10.1186/s12890-018-0593-9. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 35. Buchan K, Filannino M, Uzuner O. Automatic prediction of coronary artery disease from clinical narratives. J Biomed Inform. 2017;72:23–32. doi: 10.1016/j.jbi.2017.06.019. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 36. Castro VM, D