pproval and consent to participate The Institutional Review Board of Hadassah Medical Organization approved this study; completing questionnaires was an expression of implied consent. All methods were performed in accordance with the ethical standards as laid down in the Declaration of Helsinki and its later amendments. Competing interests The authors declare that they have no competing interests. Footnotes Publisher’s Note Springer Nature remains neutral with regard to jurisdictional claims in published maps and institutional affiliations. Contributor Information Ariel Wimpfheimer, Email: ariel.wimpfheimer@mail.huji.ac.il. the Israel Anesthesiology Workforce Study Group: Haled Abd-Al-Halim , Hakeem Abu-Rais , Chaim Berkenstadt , Ilya Chernoy , Maruan Armaly , Yaakov Duvdivani , Leonid Eidelman , Shai Fine , Brian Fredman , Yulia Gadulov , Zeev Goldik , Yaakov Gozal , Zoya Haituv , Alex Izakson , Yaakov Katz , Idit Matot , Noam Mubada , Reuven Pizov , Aeyal Raz , Gefen Revaz , Igor Reznikof , Nogzar Rigzny , Michael Rudin , Vladimir Rukinglass , Albert Sabatnitzki , Eran Segal , Eric Siton , Mustafa Somri , Riad Tome , Jacob Turban , Nathan Weksler , Dafna Wilner , Yossi Witchelevsky , and Alex Zlotnik References 1. Nagrebetsky A, Gabriel R, Dutton R, Urman R. Growth of Nonoperating room anesthesia care in the United States: a contemporary trends analysis. Anesth Analg. 2017;124:1261–2126. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 2. Louër R, Szeto M, Grasfield R, McClain CD, Urman RD, Brovman EY. Trends in pediatric non-operating room anesthesia: data from the national anesthesia clinical outcomes registry. Paediatr Anaesth. 2023;33:446–53. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 3. Weissman C, Eidelman LA, Pizov R, Matot I, Klein N, Cohn R. The Israeli anesthesiology workforce. IMAJ. 2006;8:255–60. [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 4. Sandy LG. Workforce planning—going beyond the count. Isr J Health Policy Res. 2017;6:55. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Sch