10.1007/s43678-022-00269-1. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 13. Du lanfang et al. Ge hongxia, Ma qingbian, Ge baolan, Yang jianzhong, Mi yuhong,. Practice of extracorporeal cardiopulmonary resuscitation in China after publication of the 2015 AHA guidelines for resuscitation: A multiinstitution survey. Asian Pacific Journal of Tropical Medicine. 2019;12(Suppl 2):12–16. 14. Lee CH, Chaou CH, Lin CC. The progress of emergency medicine in Taiwan, China, and Hong Kong: perspective from publications in Emergency Medicine Journals, 1992–2011. Biomed Res Int. 2014; 2014:682375. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] 15. Smith J, Date P, Spencer W, de Tonnerre E, Taylor DM. Evolution of methodology and reporting of emergency medicine quantitative research over a 20-year period. Emerg Med J. 2020;37(6):324–9. doi: 10.1136/emermed-2019-209140. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 16. Mahajan P, Visclosky T, Bhoi S, Galwankar S, Kuppermann N, Neumar R. The importance of developing global emergency medicine research network. Am J Emerg Med. 2019;37(4):744–5. doi: 10.1016/j.ajem.2018.11.032. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 17. Taneja A, Wylie T, Kalynych C, Helmi H, Fishe J. Development of a Longitudinal Research Curriculum for Pediatric Emergency Medicine Fellowship. West J Emerg Med. 2022;23(1):26–9. doi: 10.5811/westjem.2021.10.52854. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 18. Ge Hongxia Z, Yaan Z, Qi M. Comparison of emergency specialist training between American and Chinese medical colleges. Chin J Med Edu Res. 2015;14(10):986–90. [ Google Scholar ] 19. Williams AL, Blomkalns AL, Gibler WB. Residency training in emergency medicine: the challenges of the 21st century. Keio J Med. 2004;53(4):203–9. doi: 10.2302/kjm.53.203. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 20. Paxton JH, Messman AM, Harrison NE, Malik AN, Burke RJ, Levy PD. Resident Research in Emergency Medicine: an introduction and primer. West J Emerg Med. 2020;21(5):1118–22. doi: 10.58